      hu: ["A várost 1786-ban Pedro de Melo de Portugal kormányzó alapította.", "San Pedro de Ycuamandiyú San Pedro megye (a 2. megye) székhelye.", "A település távolsága a fővárostól, Asuncióntól közúton 330 km.", "A Jejuí Guazú folyó fontos vízi út volt a gyarmati időkben.", "A város híres régi kúriáiról, amelyeket 'casonas'-nak neveznek.", "A helyi gazdaság egyik fő ágazata a dohány- és gyapottermesztés.", "A város népessége a kerülettel együtt meghaladja a 35 000 főt.", "Minden június 29-én nagy ünnepséget rendeznek a város védőszentje tiszteletére."],
      ro: ["Data oficială a fondării orașului este 16 martie 1786.", "Orașul este situat la o altitudine de 115 metri peste nivelul mării.", "Districtul San Pedro de Ycuamandiyú are o suprafață de 3.165 km².", "Râul Jejuí Guazú trece la aproximativ 15 km de centrul orașului.", "Catedrala locală deține unul dintre cele mai vechi altare din lemn din țară.", "Economia departamentală este coordonată din acest centru administrativ.", "În oraș funcționează o importantă facultate de Științe Agrare.", "San Pedro de Ycuamandiyú este legat de Ruta 3 prin șoseaua PY11."],
      en: ["Founded in 1786, it is one of the oldest colonial cities in Paraguay.", "The city's name reflects both Catholic and Guaraní cultural roots.", "It is located in the central-eastern part of the Oriental Region of Paraguay.", "The city serves as the judicial and administrative seat of San Pedro Department.", "The Jejuí Guazú River near the city is famous for its white sand beaches.", "The region is a major producer of petitgrain oil, extracted from bitter orange leaves.", "Annual rainfall in San Pedro de Ycuamandiyú averages around 1,500 mm.", "The town is a key center for the traditional Paraguayan woodcarving industry."],
